Notebook[{
Cell["Film Groups", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"93a56435-f606-4c89-98b0-9e176c1e75ce"],

Cell["The 275 space-time symmetry groups of the plane, animated", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"cbeac7de-c151-44fe-81ba-47d0b2964fad"],

Cell["\<\
A film is a map from spacetime \!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\(\[DoubleStruckCapitalR]\
\), \(2\)]\)\[Times]\[DoubleStruckCapitalR] to colors. A film group is a \
crystallographic group of symmetries of such a film: transformations g : (x, \
t) \[RightArrow] (M.x + v, s\[ThinSpace]t + \[Tau]), with M a 2\[Times]2 \
point operation, v a spatial translation, s = \[PlusMinus]1 a time direction, \
and \[Tau] a time offset, containing a lattice of two independent spatial \
translations and one time period. Up to crystallographic equivalence there \
are exactly 275 such groups (Ke & Wu, arXiv:2604.05619) \[LongDash] the \
space-time analogue of the 17 wallpaper groups, and a subfamily of the 230 \
space groups read with one axis as time (Fletcher, Math. Gazette 40 (1956) 15\
\[Dash]19; the 1+1-dimensional count of 13 is in Xu & Wu, Phys. Rev. Lett. \
120, 096401 (2018)).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d9fb1f5e-edc2-4a0b-a18e-32ceaa6f1cc3"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook accompanies the FilmGroups package, a port of the interactive \
atlas at https://yaroslavvb.github.io/animated-groups-fable . Every group is \
stored as exact data, machine-verified against the group axioms, and rendered \
as a looping animation: the orbit of a single animated motif under the group.\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56160711-7e49-4d54-b366-590f825d5ebb"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d6287fc9-2e48-4079-b4ff-a148290c0df6"],

Cell["\<\
Place FilmGroups.wl and FilmGroupsData.wl in the same directory as this \
notebook and load:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5963a193-07ff-4570-b85e-d10d8622c2fa"],

Cell["\<\
SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];
Get[\"FilmGroups.wl\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"b5617fc7-3e26-44b3-9967-590850bb5bf4"],

Cell["The motif: a clock that cannot alias", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ec2c399d-887e-4914-b0ef-24d95c21e685"],

Cell["\<\
Each copy of the motif displays its own internal time \[Theta] = \
s\[ThinSpace](t \[Minus] \[Tau]): a vessel that fills once per period, its \
surface marked in red. The fill level is an injective function of \[Theta] \
mod 1, and it cannot be rotated \[LongDash] so two copies at different \
internal times always look different in a frozen frame, no matter how the \
pattern's own rotations act. Orientation and phase are independent readouts. \
The vessel is chiral and asymmetric (no accidental symmetry), and \
time-reversed copies drain instead of filling.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eac2d1f5-0a9d-4e47-9782-ef01edc54344"],

Cell["Row[Table[FilmGroupMotif[\[Theta]], {\[Theta], 0, 5/6, 1/6}], \
Spacer[4]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2456f384-8742-4b2b-8aef-6f7ec3562c8a"],

Cell["Animating a group", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"71f5350c-f479-4f01-a8c4-a8a758ccec7d"],

Cell["\<\
FilmGroupAnimation accepts an index 1\[Dash]275, an ID like \"g95\", or a \
notation symbol from the catalog. Group #95 is 4\:20824\:20822, the film \
analogue of the space group P4\:2082: a fourfold time screw \[LongDash] each \
quarter turn about a 4\:2082 centre advances the film by half a period. Press \
play.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a354a548-094b-42de-be3d-7baaf95cf9ab"],

Cell["FilmGroupAnimation[95]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"16434663-a8ea-4cc9-8d51-39db3bedcdbe"],

Cell["\<\
A hexagonal time screw, 6\:20823\:20822 (#244): the sixfold centres advance \
the film by a third of a period per sixth of a turn, so equal fill levels \
spiral around each centre.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ed4c6689-f2ae-42ee-ad52-6f16c7a521c2"],

Cell["FilmGroupAnimation[\"g244\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"816ed7f5-bb9d-48fc-90cf-a9c7303c7b0f"],

Cell["\<\
Time reversal. In o/m\[Prime][cm] (#2) a mirror runs the film backwards: \
reflected copies drain while their partners fill. Mirror pairs share a site \
and are drawn superimposed, showing both surface lines.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4759dc5c-4bf0-4e1a-adb5-20fdec459cec"],

Cell["FilmGroupAnimation[2]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"e19623e9-269f-4323-8a8f-1923f4cdc135"],

Cell["\<\
The animations are Manipulates with SaveDefinitions \[Rule] True, so they \
keep working \[LongDash] play button and all \[LongDash] in a notebook opened \
without the package.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"24c6ed2d-15e0-4b5b-b9bc-a1f7f0b44e2e"],

Cell["Window size and other options", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"43ec2762-4284-4a0c-ba44-266b7c3bc143"],

Cell["\<\
\"Cells\" sets the width of the window in lattice translations; the default \
Automatic sizes the window so roughly 16 copies are visible. \"ShowCell\" \
overlays the lattice. A frame at a single time t is a Graphics:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4abf5188-a249-4916-84e4-59aacf258f57"],

Cell["\<\
GraphicsRow[{FilmGroupFrame[95, 0.3, \"Cells\" -> 2],
  FilmGroupFrame[95, 0.3, \"Cells\" -> 4, \"ShowCell\" -> True]}, ImageSize \
-> 600]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5261aacc-466a-404c-8d9d-80a38bf844f6"],

Cell["\<\
\"MotifScale\" shrinks the stamps, \"Colors\" overrides any of \"Body\", \
\"Outline\", \"Fill\", \"Line\", \"Background\", and Background and ImageSize \
pass through to Graphics.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"000e9bda-bd17-4973-a306-0667761b0d28"],

Cell["\<\
FilmGroupFrame[258, 0.25, \"Cells\" -> {6, 3}, \"MotifScale\" -> 0.9,
  \"Colors\" -> <|\"Fill\" -> RGBColor[\"#8c4a3a\"], \"Line\" -> \
RGBColor[\"#1a3a5c\"]|>,
  ImageSize -> 640]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ba4219ce-3e58-4df4-9511-0497913e8428"],

Cell["Browsing all 275", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"11679552-b27a-49be-a432-8af7d26add23"],

Cell["\<\
The browser steps through the whole catalog (requires the package loaded in \
the current session):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1342abce-4119-48b1-9fd7-77cab91d26e1"],

Cell["FilmGroupBrowser[]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0975e78c-8059-481f-86e0-5a042da2a5b8"],

Cell["The catalog", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b2e96780-911d-4068-bc6c-80624b038780"],

Cell["\<\
FilmGroupData[] is the full catalog as a Dataset. Each entry records the \
notation Symbol (Conway orbifold notation with time decorations: gyration \
subscripts n\:2096 for time screws, \[Tilde] for time glides, \[Prime] for \
time reversal, c/r prefixes for space-time-centred lattices \[LongDash] see \
the atlas notation page), the crystal System, the base wallpaper group of the \
spatial projection, the flags ForwardTime / Product / Symmorphic, \
human-readable Generators, and the exact rendering spec (Basis, Ops, \
BasePoint).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4ae07742-e38d-4ae3-95be-07b3abb74013"],

Cell["FilmGroupData[]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a1f1cc63-80df-4294-b3a6-3f26a692280b"],

Cell["Normal @ FilmGroupData[][GroupBy[\"System\"], Length]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a51c5d37-bce4-4e25-a3db-4ee310141fbd"],

Cell["\<\
FilmGroupData[][Select[#ForwardTime && ! #Symmorphic &], Length]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ffe86720-45aa-433a-9a44-0c2d0a086433"],

Cell["Column @ FilmGroupData[95, \"Generators\"]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8480eecd-fece-4b92-9890-7539d7d76baf"],

Cell["Verified symmetry", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f62ed750-112f-41ba-886c-164c6bfc12c7"],

Cell["\<\
\"Ops\" lists coset representatives of the group modulo \!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\
\(\[DoubleStruckCapitalZ]\), \(2\)]\)\[Times]\[DoubleStruckCapitalZ] (lattice \
and time period), stored exactly \[LongDash] integer matrices, rational \
offsets, Sqrt[3]/2. VerifyFilmGroup checks identity, inverses and closure in \
exact arithmetic. The whole catalog passes:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8065dd84-e77c-4997-acc0-7ed3e75709e3"],

Cell["AllTrue[Range[275], VerifyFilmGroup[#][\"OK\"] &]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0fb7a8ad-f75b-416d-b34e-824c994ef420"],

Cell["\<\
Rendering then inherits the symmetry by construction: a frame is drawn as the \
explicit orbit of the base motif under these representatives and the lattice, \
so applying any listed operation to the picture at time t reproduces the \
picture at time s\[ThinSpace]t + \[Tau] exactly.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d655a5ae-4b67-49e1-aba5-b675454a6aae"],

Cell["Exporting", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"48f67792-7b8f-4f75-b12d-e1a75f35a5f4"],

Cell["\<\
Frames export to an animated GIF (here 40 frames, 4 seconds per period, \
matching the atlas):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6dbccdc5-288e-4bca-8b09-eff6a0fa2137"],

Cell["\<\
Export[\"film-group-95.gif\", FilmGroupFrames[95, 40, ImageSize -> 320],
  \"DisplayDurations\" -> 0.1, \"AnimationRepetitions\" -> Infinity]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"4089b1f1-eb9f-4423-a6d4-381adc2c46d2"],

Cell["References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a4699cda-4e81-41e4-978e-a076164ed311"],

Cell["\<\
T. J. Fletcher, Film groups, Math. Gazette 40 (1956) 15\[Dash]19.
Ke & Wu, Space-time groups in 2+1 dimensions, arXiv:2604.05619.
Xu & Wu, Space-time crystals in 1+1 dimensions, Phys. Rev. Lett. 120, 096401 \
(2018).
J. H. Conway, H. Burgiel, C. Goodman-Strauss, The Symmetries of Things (2008) \
\[LongDash] orbifold notation.
Interactive atlas: https://yaroslavvb.github.io/animated-groups-fable
Source: https://github.com/yaroslavvb/animated-groups-fable (wolfram/ \
directory; the catalog data is generated from the atlas's own, and both \
renderers agree frame by frame).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8f78cf19-ae61-4cfa-a148-4c90944abe70"]
},
WindowSize->{900, 800},
FrontEndVersion->"14.2 for Mac OS X x86 (64-bit) (March 16, 2025)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"12be45a1-e2d3-4d62-a1f2-b340c3511b79"
]
(* End of Notebook Content *)

